    "image_with_text_cH4gbB": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_6YanU4": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "A Taste of the North Highlands",
            "size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_qp8cgC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>At the heart of Dunrobin Gin is a carefully balanced selection of botanicals, chosen to reflect the gardens, woodland and natural beauty of the Scottish Highlands.</p><p>Juniper, lemon, coriander, and angelica root form the foundation of our gin, complemented by clove and rose-scented pelargonium and blackcurrant leaves, both carefully grown and harvested from the gardens of Dunrobin Castle.</p><p>Together, these botanicals create a distinctive Scottish gin with earthy, piney and gently spiced notes, balanced by a delicate floral freshness.</p><p>From the formal gardens of Dunrobin Castle to the rolling hills of Sutherland and the coastline overlooking the Moray Firth, every element of Dunrobin Gin reflects the remarkable landscape that surrounds us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button_xhPeJ8": {
